	(text "CR-3 - ISOLATED HIGH-SIDE SUPPLY FOR THE AMC1311 (TI SBAS786C section 10).\nWHY THIS STAGE EXISTS: U702 previously drew VIN/GND from VGD_LS_P / VGD_LS_COM,\nwhich are the power module LOW-SIDE KELVIN SOURCE pins.  A Kelvin sense node\nmust never carry supply current: at 4 kA/us through ~8 nH of module source\ninductance the Kelvin pair and DC_BUS_N differ by tens of volts on every edge,\nand that transient appeared directly inside the AMC1311 supply loop.\nU704 (SN6505B, free-running: EN tied to VCC, CLK to GND) drives T701 from the\ncontrol-side +5 V.  D701/D702 form a centre-tapped full-wave rectifier whose\nreturn is DC_BUS_N; C713 is the reservoir; U702 then post-regulates to 3V3_HV.\nEVERYTHING on the secondary side references DC_BUS_N - C713, U702 GND, C701,\nC702, C706, C707, U701 GND1 and the divider bottom R705 are one single node.\nLoad is only the AMC1311 IDD1 <= 8.4 mA, so 1:1.1 x 5 V - 2 diode-drop margin\nleaves ~5.1 V raw, comfortably above the MCP1804 3.3 V dropout.\nT701 IS THE REINFORCED BARRIER ELEMENT of this stage: Wurth 750313734,\nreinforced 800 Vrms / 1400 Vpk per IEC62368-1, 5000 Vrms hipot, 9.2 mm creepage\nand 8.0 mm clearance PRI-SEC per IEC61800-5-1.  Keep the board cut-out / keepout\nunder T701 aligned with the SPEC 10 barrier - no copper, no silk, no plane\ncrossing between the primary (1,2,3) and secondary (6,5,4) rows.\nA 2.5 kV-class functional-isolation part (e.g. 760390012) must NOT be substituted."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
